---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---
<Marketing
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Total Recall handles your data: your brain lives in infrastructure you own, and the theo app is built so we cannot read your memory."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(32px,4.6vw,52px);margin:10px 0 0">Your memory is yours.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin:18px 0 0">
        Total Recall is built around one architectural promise: your brain, meaning the database
        that holds your documents, messages, contacts, and everything derived from them, runs in
        accounts you own. We designed the product so we cannot read it.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top:40px;display:grid;gap:28px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65">
        <p style="color:var(--muted,#666);margin:0">Effective date: July 12, 2026</p>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Where your data lives</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            When you set up a brain, the setup wizard deploys it into your own accounts: a Postgres
            database (the storage engine) in your Supabase account, always-on services in your
            Railway account, and AI processing billed to your own OpenAI and Anthropic keys. Your
            documents, emails, chat messages, contacts, and the memory built from them are stored
            there, under your logins, on infrastructure you can inspect, export, or delete without
            our involvement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">What we store</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            The theo app (this website and the setup wizard at asktheo.totalrecallhq.com) keeps the
            minimum it needs to function: your account identity from sign-in (name and email, via
            our sign-in provider Clerk), your setup progress (which steps you completed and your
            setup questionnaire answers), and standard operational logs. That is the list.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">What we deliberately do not store</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            The wizard is a zero-credential router. The API keys, database passwords, and tokens you
            paste during setup are used transiently, meaning we check them and pass them directly to
            your own infrastructure without writing them to our systems; between steps they live
            only in your browser tab. When you connect a source through a Total Recall hosted app
            (for example our Slack app), the resulting access token is delivered straight to your
            own services and is never stored on ours. Your brain's contents never pass through our
            servers at all: search and chat happen between your devices, your brain, and your AI
            provider accounts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">The services involved</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Running theo involves a small set of third parties, each with a narrow job: Clerk
            (sign-in), Vercel (hosting this app), and the providers of accounts you own and connect
            yourself, such as Supabase, Railway, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Slack, Notion, and
            Telegram. Sources you connect are governed by the permissions you grant on those
            platforms, and you can revoke them there at any time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">AI processing and training</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Your content is processed by AI models using your own OpenAI and Anthropic accounts,
            under those providers' API terms, which by default do not use API content to train
            models. We never use your content to train anything, and we could not: we do not have
            it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Deleting your data</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Because your brain lives in your accounts, deletion is genuinely in your hands: deleting
            your Supabase project and Railway services removes the data and stops the billing, and
            our guides walk through an orderly export first if you want one. To remove what we hold,
            email us and we will delete your account identity and setup records.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Changes and contact</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            If this policy changes, we will update this page and its effective date. Questions,
            deletion requests, or anything unclear: <a href="mailto:support@totalrecallhq.com">support@totalrecallhq.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
